[{:db/id "q-110537/selection/edc901e84f0cdd5174afd49105ac3883566ea0e1e057217fb66083a56cc119ba" :answer/id #uuid "0b48d8dc-25ee-5188-abc9-a2f92b13f2c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110537/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "b001678a-1c1a-5dce-a7b0-9d3ab17a6ef0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110537/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "f4c807df-e71e-5a4f-af92-24d496440270" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110537/selection/d3a7133ef1a1f6526aaec763d522f5ae075d8386a4606de90dcb93094f1d21d6" :answer/id #uuid "d0b5ffec-635f-54a1-92e0-765a82a62284" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110537/selection/25666b67a56594dd5245ec05e89d883db07d04362ab51dbc90c39ad20f7f9142" :answer/id #uuid "7c79d5ea-620d-5f46-8e2a-0cc77b8a5a54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110537/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "41fa3146-0439-526f-8a2b-79cf92f3b238" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110537/selection/edc901e84f0cdd5174afd49105ac3883566ea0e1e057217fb66083a56cc119ba" :answer-field/choices ["q-110537/selection/edc901e84f0cdd5174afd49105ac3883566ea0e1e057217fb66083a56cc119ba" "q-110537/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-110537/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" "q-110537/selection/d3a7133ef1a1f6526aaec763d522f5ae075d8386a4606de90dcb93094f1d21d6" "q-110537/selection/25666b67a56594dd5245ec05e89d883db07d04362ab51dbc90c39ad20f7f9142"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110537" :question/id #uuid "028d8773-8ea7-5c3f-b517-f8c76313f6d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-110537" :question/is-example false :question/problem "If ${4}^{k-1}={64}^{2k}$ then $k=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this equation, we need both exponential terms to have a common base.\n\nTo do this, we write $64$ as ${4}^{3},$ and then rewrite the left-hand side using the power rule of exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{4}^{k-1} & ={64}^{2k} \\\\ {4}^{k-1} & ={({4}^{3})}^{2k} \\\\ {4}^{k-1} & ={4}^{6k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(4),$ we equate the exponents and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k-1 & =6k \\\\ -1 & =5k \\\\ k & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-110537/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c6b30e7-fba6-597c-8306-27d707bfc244"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110537"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-100449/selection/d3a7133ef1a1f6526aaec763d522f5ae075d8386a4606de90dcb93094f1d21d6" :answer/id #uuid "f51a2a9d-aa08-59d2-8de3-146721680d3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100449/selection/1f5b353af7cbb90a89e4a07f196cff5b0ba27d9934d00e9a38de61eff80108f7" :answer/id #uuid "618a3d18-0334-5e5f-bf2e-a11a27c6998c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100449/selection/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8" :answer/id #uuid "44e9f8c5-1f0d-51b1-a537-e42625d748c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100449/selection/2b998a440c758092569557828849b9a2d05282247ea8a11a5727b6cadcbcb080" :answer/id #uuid "4c595474-8fe6-5c9f-9e44-93e1d33b3a88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100449/selection/4582dbd6025ba0c110f8e23964efc62e8612751348ffad003e8834a5780c1878" :answer/id #uuid "a877d75f-1f12-58f4-83b1-1138231651f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-100449/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5a1fe442-8b64-5d08-a6c0-bdfcd15919c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-100449/selection/4582dbd6025ba0c110f8e23964efc62e8612751348ffad003e8834a5780c1878" :answer-field/choices ["q-100449/selection/d3a7133ef1a1f6526aaec763d522f5ae075d8386a4606de90dcb93094f1d21d6" "q-100449/selection/1f5b353af7cbb90a89e4a07f196cff5b0ba27d9934d00e9a38de61eff80108f7" "q-100449/selection/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8" "q-100449/selection/2b998a440c758092569557828849b9a2d05282247ea8a11a5727b6cadcbcb080" "q-100449/selection/4582dbd6025ba0c110f8e23964efc62e8612751348ffad003e8834a5780c1878"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-100449" :question/id #uuid "78892017-6fcd-5bd8-a72d-1a9de112b877" :question/math-academy-id "q-100449" :question/is-example false :question/problem "If ${8}^{5a-12}=\\frac{1}{{64}^{a+4}}$ then $a=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this equation, we need both exponential terms to have a common base.\n\nTo do this, we write $64$ as ${8}^{2},$ and then we rewrite the right-hand side using the power rule of exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{8}^{5a-12} & =\\frac{1}{{64}^{a+4}} \\\\ {8}^{5a-12} & =\\frac{1}{{({8}^{2})}^{a+4}} \\\\ {8}^{5a-12} & =\\frac{1}{{8}^{2(a+4)}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using a negative exponent: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{8}^{5a-12} & ={8}^{-2(a+4)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(8)$, we equate the exponents and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5a-12 & =-2(a+4) \\\\ 5a-12 & =-2a-8 \\\\ 7a & =4 \\\\ a & =\\frac{4}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-100449/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c6b30e7-fba6-597c-8306-27d707bfc244"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-100449"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-66872/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "9af43b97-de5e-5c8b-a678-9e5e131daed2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66872/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "63fa4516-a843-537e-8b2d-1142c5eb61f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66872/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "5c0a1dcf-e190-50e9-913c-469efdc27f08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66872/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "b35782de-0cb8-55cd-a950-22ae5ca81e40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66872/selection/283bc09f1a097ae8400558511ca45f1013e17c797fdb7407be52694190fd744b" :answer/id #uuid "64762fea-4f3c-5c6a-a843-1ab71507f8ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66872/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d4c5e5e8-7f85-5156-ac98-78e9427f57b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-66872/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer-field/choices ["q-66872/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-66872/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-66872/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" "q-66872/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-66872/selection/283bc09f1a097ae8400558511ca45f1013e17c797fdb7407be52694190fd744b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-66872" :question/id #uuid "3ebf6c1e-0a48-59c4-947a-b6b73359a717" :question/math-academy-id "q-66872" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Solve for $m$ where ${5}^{m-10}={125}^{m}.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this equation, we need both exponential terms to have a common base.\n\nTo do this, we write $125$ as ${5}^{3},$ and then rewrite the right-hand side using the power rule of exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{m-10} & ={125}^{m} \\\\ {5}^{m-10} & ={({5}^{3})}^{m} \\\\ {5}^{m-10} & ={5}^{3m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(5)$, we equate the exponents and solve for $m:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m-10 & =3m \\\\ -2m & =10 \\\\ m & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-66872/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c6b30e7-fba6-597c-8306-27d707bfc244"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-66872"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-66863/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "f5e42810-88ae-5580-abe2-048b3b43057f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66863/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "4c6597ff-0956-5ccb-af41-dd28a72f5ec4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66863/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "a4675094-4fbb-5581-b921-d6fa1249323c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66863/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "3123609b-b7b4-5724-af39-26f02d5fd33c" :answer/type :answer.type/mat